.TH PREAD 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
pread \- read bytes at a file offset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B ssize_t pread(int descriptor, void* buffer, size_t byte_count, off_t offset);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads bytes at offset without changing the open file's current position.
Reads may be short; the caller must provide sufficient writable storage.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes read, zero at EOF, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pwrite (3crunch),
.BR read (3crunch),
.BR pread (2)
